# Live desktop run metrics
Workstream-ID: lea-20
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/20
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: Reviewed execution paths and fictional offline fixtures
Status: DONE
Milestone: Show current-command outcomes while automation is running
Dependencies: lea-11, lea-18, lea-19

## Purpose
Show readable, color-coded per-command counters beside the running console
instead of requiring the final summary. Cover Apply, Scan, Reapply and Connect;
distinguish confirmed applications, inspected jobs, skips, failures, actual
hiring-team messages, drafts, dry-run outcomes and connection invitations.
Keep existing automation decisions, prompts, saved configuration and history
unchanged. Do not attach to or manipulate an independently running window.

## Tasks
- [x] Trace authoritative outcomes and define an explicit progress contract.
- [x] Stream progress separately from human-readable log formatting.
- [x] Add responsive themed counters, target progress and elapsed time.
- [x] Preserve counters after completion/stop and reset only for a new command.
- [x] Exercise producer-to-window updates and important negative cases offline.
- [x] Update directly affected guides and fictional visual references.
- [x] Independently verify the scoped issue, Project item and backlink.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Counters update before a long-running command finishes.
- [x] All four run actions expose their appropriate current-command metrics.
- [x] Attempts, dry runs, drafts and uncertain submissions never inflate sent totals.
- [x] Clear log, theme changes and command-selector edits do not corrupt live totals.
- [x] Compact layouts remain readable without squeezing out the run controls.
- [x] Streaming prompts, input forwarding and existing log presentation are preserved.
- [x] Tests use disposable state and do not manipulate the user's active instance.
- [x] Existing work, tracking records, private settings and released binaries remain intact.
- [x] Offline evidence is distinct from live qualification, human acceptance and publication.

## Completion evidence
Local implementation and bounded offline qualification are complete.
Strict status-only snapshots connect authoritative engine outcomes to five
responsive themed cards, target progress and elapsed time. Apply, Scan and
Reapply show scanned/applied/skipped/failed/HR-sent totals; Connect shows
profiles/invitations/already/skipped/failed. Drafts, completed dry runs,
uncertainty and invitation outcomes remain separate from actual sends.

The affected engine, child-process, five GUI suites and desktop integration
passed 308 tests with native exit zero. Black/Ruff passed fifteen scoped
Python files; mypy passed sixteen source files. Real-child fixtures verify
updates before exit, input forwarding, finish/stop/reset and invalid-frame
recovery. Font-aware geometry/help checks pass compact and expanded sizes in
both themes. These tests are not live automation or installed-build qualification.

Thirteen affected guides are synchronized without expanding the short README.
Seven Run PNGs and the nine-frame, 17.8-second Run GIF use explicit fictional
snapshots; no child or elapsed timer starts for media. Sampled offscreen
inspection covers compact light and expanded dark layouts. Twenty-eight unrelated
public fingerprints, nineteen previous durable mappings, selected private/native
metadata, HEAD and the empty staged diff match the immutable baseline.

The initial issue/Project/backlink was independently verified; completion
settlement is a separate receipt outside this managed body. The source remains
local and uncommitted. The existing released executable and user window are
not rebuilt, replaced, inspected or restarted. A shared source checkout is not
a frozen protected build. Human acceptance and new live qualification remain
unclaimed. Existing application/outreach persistence and final-summary ordering
are preserved: live observed outcomes can precede their durable recording.

## Completion log
- 2026-11-09: Completed typed telemetry, responsive counters and lifecycle
  handling. Final integrated qualification passed 308 cases after correcting
  a capture-fixture assertion that treated a stale Reapply-only option as
  active during Connect. Earlier compact checks exposed missing headless
  fonts and then genuine header clipping; registered real fonts and made
  the caption responsive instead of weakening geometry assertions.
- 2026-11-09: Refreshed directly affected guides and fictional Run media.
  Preserved prior source work, selected private/native metadata and tracking.
  No live browsing, application, outreach, invitation, release, commit, push
  or user-process manipulation was performed.
- 2026-11-09: Started bounded live desktop metrics. Preserve the existing
  tooltip, console and README work; inspect actual execution outcomes before
  choosing counters. Scope includes local source, focused checks, affected
  documentation/media and reviewed issue/Project tracking, not publication.
